  recipeId: led
  concept: 'Authored objective: Red LED Conducting.

    Authored requirement: Red
    SparkLED must be forward biased and conducting; fixed binding ID led. Connection
    pair LED_Anode and LED_Cathode. Conduction required.

    General teaching principle:
    An LED has a defined anode and cathode; correct polarity and suitable current
    control matter for normal forward operation.

    Only fresh, authoritative game
    evidence can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A directional gate with a current limit is a useful model, although an
    LED is not an ideal one-way switch.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A lit LED alone does not establish that its current and power are
    within safe ratings.
